# Precision Fixes for Import Bill Pipeline

These changes improve the accuracy and data completeness of the AI-powered Import Bill feature.

## Proposed Changes

### AI Parser Core

#### [MODIFY] [aiParser.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock pro/lib/aiParser.ts)

**1. Add `normalizeExpiryDate()` function** (after [normalizePacking](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#542-572))
- Converts `MMM-YY` → `YYYY-MM-DD` (last day of month, pharmacy standard)
- Examples: `Sep-26` → `2026-09-30`, `Feb-28` → `2028-02-28`, `Nov-25` → `2025-11-30`

**2. Add `ptr` and `cashDiscount` to [ParsedMedicine](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/medicine/import-price-list.tsx#48-65) interface**
- `ptr`: Price to Retailer (reference price)
- `cashDiscount`: CD% column value

**3. Update [normalizeMedicine()](file:///C:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#150-183) to handle new fields**
- Parse `ptr`, `cashDiscount` from AI output
- Call `normalizeExpiryDate()` on `expiryDate`

**4. Rewrite `INVOICE_IMAGE_PROMPT`** (remove Ayukalp-specific hardcoding)
- Generalize for ANY Indian Ayurvedic invoice
- Explicitly map: `purchaseRate = PTS`, `ptr = PTR`, `mrp = MRP`
- Add CD% extraction
- Add invoice metadata extraction (invoiceNumber, invoiceDate, supplierName)

**5. Update [normalizeMedicines()](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts#573-583) to apply expiry normalization**

